//! A fuzzer-found, minimised Parquet reproducer for the parquet-metadata
//! `byte_range` panic (#52), committed **as source** (a `const &[u8]`), not
//! as an opaque binary blob — the repo "no committed binary blob" convention.
//!
//! # Provenance
//!
//! `fuzz_parquet_feed` produced a crash that `cargo fuzz tmin` minimised to
//! these bytes. Before the #52 catch_unwind backstop, feeding them to
//! `ParquetFeed::open` **panicked** inside parquet during row-group decode:
//! `ColumnChunkMetaData::byte_range()` asserts `col_start >= 0 && col_len >= 0`
//! (parquet-59.1.0 file/metadata/mod.rs:1063), and a crafted negative
//! column-chunk offset trips it — a member of the parquet metadata-panic
//! class arrow-rs is still patching (PRs #9840, #9868, #5382). The fix wraps
//! the upstream builder/decode calls in `std::panic::catch_unwind` at both
//! Parquet read sites, so the panic is contained and mapped to a typed
//! `BacktestError` (never an unwind).
//!
//! Faithful in-Rust synthesis of a negative-offset column chunk is impractical
//! (parquet's own writer will not emit one), so the minimised reproducer is
//! embedded verbatim — deterministic, reviewable, source-pinned. The permanent
//! regression is the no-panic assertion in `tests/security.rs`.
//!
//! sha256 = 88826f7c3087914247a2da3393a67a9f81d75d86f75eaa36d843236378cd52e2
//! length = 3884 bytes

